Subject: [PATCH] cosmic-greeter/locker: idle at startup without logind instead
 of locking immediately

LeandrOS has no logind (no org.freedesktop.login1). cosmic-greeter is therefore
built with `--no-default-features` (the `logind` default feature would make the
locker subscribe to logind on the zbus system bus and `std::process::exit(1)`
when the service is absent -> infinite crash-loop under cosmic-session's restart
supervision).

But the non-logind arm of `locker::init()` is equally unusable as-is: it locks
the screen IMMEDIATELY at process start, and after a successful unlock the
`SessionLockEvent::Unlocked` handler calls `process::exit(0)`. cosmic-session
spawns the greeter/locker in-session with infinite restart + exponential
backoff, so the sequence becomes: start -> lock -> unlock -> exit(0) -> restart
-> lock -> ... i.e. the desktop can never stay unlocked.

This patch changes ONLY the non-logind startup arm to mirror the logind arm:
lock at startup only when recovering a previously-locked session (the lock file
exists), otherwise `Task::none()` (idle). On LeandrOS nothing triggers a lock
at boot, so the locker starts idle and stays out of the way; the wallpaper/panel
session runs normally. A lock can still be requested explicitly (Message::Lock),
and recovery of a crashed locked session still works via the lock file.

Residual behavior after this patch: because the non-logind `Unlocked` handler
still `process::exit(0)`s, an actual unlock exits the process; cosmic-session
restarts it, and it now comes back IDLE (no lock file present) rather than
re-locking. That is the intended, startup-safe behavior.

This is the only .rs change made to cosmic-greeter for LeandrOS. Apply against
the vendored source tree (byte-identical to upstream cosmic-epoch/cosmic-greeter
at rsync time):

    ~/code/leandros-artifacts/m6-session-bins/src/cosmic-greeter

Build with build-rust.sh (musl toolchain) using `--no-default-features` so the
root `cosmic-greeter` binary is produced; link resolves libpam.so.0 (the
LeandrOS libpam shim, src/libpam-shim) from the m3 sysroot.

--- a/src/locker.rs
+++ b/src/locker.rs
@@ -689,11 +689,19 @@
                 // When logind feature is used, wait for lock signal
                 Task::none()
             }
-        } else {
-            // When logind feature not used, lock immediately
-            tracing::info!("locking immediately");
+        } else if already_locked {
+            // LeandrOS: without logind there is no external lock trigger, so
+            // mirror the logind branch — only lock at startup when recovering a
+            // previously-locked session (lock file present).
+            tracing::info!("recovering previous locked state");
             app.state = State::Locking;
             lock()
+        } else {
+            // LeandrOS: do NOT lock immediately. Upstream's non-logind arm locks
+            // at boot (and, with the process::exit(0) after unlock plus
+            // cosmic-session's restart, relocks forever). With no logind lock
+            // signal on LeandrOS, a fresh start must idle instead.
+            Task::none()
         };

         (app, Task::batch([task, common_task]))
